===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*keh₂p-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|LL.|praeceptum}}, form of {{m|la|praecipiō||to teach}}, from {{der|en|la|prae||pre-}} + {{m|la|capiō||take}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɹiːsɛpt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-precept.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːsɛpt|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[rule]] or [[principle]], especially one governing [[personal]] [[conduct]].
#: {{ux|en|Precept guides, but example draws.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2006|author=[[w:Anthony Daniels (psychiatrist)|Theodore Dalrymple]]|url=http://www.city-journal.org/html/16_4_urbanities-language.html|title=The Gift of Language
|passage=I need hardly point out that Pinker doesn't really believe anything of what he writes, at least if example is stronger evidence of belief than '''precept'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1891|author=Susan Hale|title=Mexico|series=The Story of the Nations|volume=27|location=London|publisher=T. Fisher Unwin|page=80|passage=He found a people in the extreme of barbarism living in caves, feeding upon the bloody flesh of animals they killed in hunting; he taught them many things, so that by his example, and for generations after he left them by his '''precepts''', they advanced to high civilization.}}
# {{lb|en|legal}} A [[written]] [[command]], especially a [[demand]] for [[payment]].
# {{lb|en|UK}}  An order issued by one local authority to another specifying the rate of tax to be charged on its behalf.
## A rate or tax set by a precept.
##* {{ux|en|The Parish Council is financed by raising a small levy - the '''precept''' - on all residential properties within the parish. [http://www.medsteadpc.org/community/medstead-parish-council-12575/home]}}

